 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "What does it express?",
   "texto": [
    "The passive one puts in the foreground what gets the action or the result, and often leaves without saying who did it: ∞ **열어요** = open the door; ∞ **열려요** = the door opens / is open (depending on context). Not all forms describe something that happens «alone»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common",
   "texto": [
    "Algunos verbos forman una pasiva con **-이-, -히-, -리-** o **-기-**: 열다 → **열리다**, 닫다 → **닫히다**, 잡다 → **잡히다**, 듣다 → **들리다**. The suffix cannot be deduced safely: each couple learns and its use. Other verbs have a passive lexic form of their own."
   ]
  },
